{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/182293-exorcise-a-demon-or-more-exactly-freeing-a-cover","id":182293,"title":"\"Exorcise a Demon\"- or more exactly, freeing a Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-27T15:51:47-07:00","id":182293,"title":"\"Exorcise a Demon\"- or more exactly, freeing a Cover","content":"so, something random I thought about while I took a shower..<br /> <br /> In order to get a control over a Cover, a demon must make a pact, preferably, a Soul Pact. Doing so, would allow the Demon to take the person wholly, with the Soul just being an &quot;anchor&quot; for the deal- the demon doesn't need it after the Pact is complete and even throws it away afterward, but without it the Pact is meaningless (I remember that if the one bound to the demon lose his Soul, the demon can't take over the Cover until he finds his lost one/ gets a new one).<br /> <br /> Now, assuming that the way demons see a &quot;soul&quot; is the same way the GMC and Mage interpreted it (and not the way games like Geist do), could it mean that if, one way or another, someone takes a soul and stuff it back into a Cover, would the demon's hold over the Cover would be broken, and he'll be forced out of it? And now, with a new soul, the demon would have to try and bind the Pact again if he would like to take the Cover back? (sure, there aren't many things outside of mages and demons which can manipulate souls that way, but still).<br /> <br /> your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:54:03-07:00","id":182599,"title":"","content":"Well since for a demon to take the cover the original person ceases to exist, I'd say hypothetically even if a demon managed to take the identity of a soulless person, which I don't think they can do anyway, the soul would cease to exist.<br /> <br /> Not that a demon sharing a body with a person is impossible. For example, their exploit to become a ghost or spirit as a cover. While they don't gain access to numina or influences, they do gain access to manifestations, and that means a demon in spirit or ghost form can possess someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-28-2014, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T00:44:22-07:00","id":182688,"title":"","content":"Well, I actually meant stuffing a new soul into the Cover (because in the way a &quot;soul&quot; is presented in the GMC and Mage, it is a replaceable thing. You just take it from someone else or something)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T02:40:25-07:00","id":182746,"title":"","content":"I think there would be no such possibility since the person is essentially erased from existence\u2026unless the Contract itself was destroyed somehow. At which point I would imagine that the Demon would immediately lose the pact's cover while the originally lost person would materialize somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T17:38:25-07:00","id":184236,"title":"","content":"It was my understanding that, much like with a gadget, when a Demon makes good on a Soul Pact, they do not actually take the soul or even the body. The body does not become a Cover, but instead is completely erased from existence, along with the soul of the original occupant and then emboldened with this new cosmic hole in creation the Demon is able to fit themselves into that hole. This is the reason that while a Soul Pact is very good, it isn't <i>perfect</i> and thus doesn't start at 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:03:31-07:00","id":184477,"title":"","content":"I thought the soul was destroyed in a Soul Pact, not just shunted out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:46:30-07:00","id":184518,"title":"","content":"Oh okay, that's a very different premise.<br /> <br /> If someone like a mage stuffs a soul into a demon, well I don't think the result would be anything good, although probably not as bad as the idea of stuffing a soul into a promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:25:03-07:00","id":184543,"title":"","content":"...Huh. I just realized something.<br /> <br /> Demons are fallen Angels, servants of the God-Machine, and they can destroy souls. <i>Qashmallim</i> are Angels of The Principle, and they steer the Azoth within Prometheans in order to <i>create</i> souls. A further bit of the Gnostic relationship between the Purpose and the Principle or just happy coincidence? You decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:32:17-07:00","id":184549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the case of soul pacts, however, it is not just a part, but the entirety of a person\u2019s existence. They are annihilated from the universe mind, body and soul, gone beyond recall of any of a demon\u2019s magics. Perhaps there are some forces in the universe that can recall a person destroyed this way, but such vast cosmic powers are beyond the scope of a demon character. Destroying the actual contract which binds the soul may return the destroyed person to existence, but if this is true, no demon has ever verified it. Such pacts are the most closely guarded of a demon\u2019s contracts. The promise of a way back for a loved one or even a hated enemy (upon whom vengeance is no longer an option) might make an interesting basis for a chronicle, however, even if the rumor comes on the lips of a demon. </div> </div> </div>From the Demon core. It's looking like souls in a Soul Pact are annihilated, not just driven from the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T03:50:48-07:00","id":184714,"title":"","content":"The way I read it is...it's not necessarily just the soul that you're taking out. The soul only does so much in a character; it's not the seat of your intelligence, your decision-making, etc. There's something beyond the soul, which I'm going to call the self, that exists separate from the soul. Even a thrall isn't a fully catatonic meat sack - there's still -something- in there behind the wheel driving him or her to do what they do.<br /> <br /> When you call in a soul pact, you're essentially shearing not only that soul out, but all that self, that driving force as well. Once all that's removed, who they are doesn't exist, only who they are <i>in relation to other people and things</i>. The demon takes this fully formed suit of contexts and identifying markers and wears it as it's new skin, hopefully fitting in well enough to cause minimal fuss to the relationships the cover has, thus <i>minimizing damage to it</i>.<br /> <br /> I'll reiterate that again, because it's an important thing to note: the <i>entirety</i> of what's left of the person is it's physical identifying characteristics - it's appearance, it's voice, etc - and the context it holds with other people and things. You didn't just replace the engine on the car, you somehow removed the paintjob, the tags and the VIN and slapped it all on another chassis. And if that paintjob doesn't fit with the chassis or someone notices that the VIN turns up something different in the registry...well, that's what compromise is.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean, obviously do what you want with your games, YMMV and all that, I'm just trying to lay out the text as I understand it as a baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 06-30-2014, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}